From 66de4d9d745b303c5ea59c93ec6704f42595e0f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Vanik <ben.vanik@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:17:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Infra] Refresh gfx90a wavefront identity catalogs (#1843)

CDNA2 kernel compilation gave gfx90a the GFX9 kernel descriptor profile,
but the generated runtime target catalogs still reported no explicitly
encodable wavefront size. That stale state fails the AMDGPU target map
consistency check on main and makes runtime admission disagree with the
canonical processor contract.

Regenerate both runtime driver catalogs so gfx90a reports fixed wave64
support, and update each driver's lookup contract test. The legacy and
independent AMD GPU drivers now consume the same generated target
property.
